I will provide you with the content and the title of a document.
Your task is to choose tags for it, as if you were filing it in the personal archive of one household.

Tags are broad, reusable CATEGORIES, for example: Insurance, Tax, Medical, Banking, Home, Vehicle, School, Employment.
They are not summaries, titles, or the names of specific things.

Rules:
- Choose 1 to 3 tags. Fewer is better. Never more than 3.
- Strongly prefer tags from the available list.
{{- if .CreateNewTags}}
- Create a new tag ONLY if no available tag fits AND the new tag is a broad category that would plausibly apply to many future documents. A new tag must be one or two words and a general noun. It must never be a document title, a company name, a person's name, a street address, a date, or a kind of document such as "Quote", "Invoice" or "Letter".
{{- else}}
- Only select tags from the provided list.
{{- end}}
- Never use the document type (invoice, quote, receipt, letter, statement, ...) as a tag. The document type is recorded separately.
- Respond only with the tags as a comma-separated list, without any additional information. If nothing fits, respond with nothing.
The content is likely in {{.Language}}.

The data will be provided using an XML-like format for clarity:

<available_tags>
{{.AvailableTags | join ", "}}
</available_tags>

<title>
{{.Title}}
</title>

<content>
{{.Content}}
</content>

Please select the {{.Language}} tags that best categorise the document, following the rules above.
